l91cGxvYWRlZF90aHVtYm5haWwuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=dc9dOXmZH_IQ7kNvwGKwaV8&_nc_oc=AdoT5M3io3DifkwKG0TyAo7EXunkxkRkNaFPnEkF8Hy5WcJyOvvBMIiQYpjqN5D3HwE&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=epynMy4urCwlMuxxEkPg4g&_nc_ss=70689&oh=00_AQQ0qWzpGZiBii7wEKTN3qxqG0hNiZd9hXw9xNt5B3IRCg&oe=6AF7ED21", "width": 360, "height": 640, "id": "9", "resolution": "360x640"}], "comments": [{"author": "drippy_wooo", "author_id": "54335518873", "id": "18114587522165677", "text": "Abhimanya ka revenge finely completed 🙌", "timestamp": 1794242187, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "vedastovikings", "author_id": "60997589521", "id": "18204117796376144", "text": "@aikantik07 Thanks for clarifying. In the BORI Critical Edition (Drona Parva 7.121.15-16) the sun is simply about to set when Arjuna strikes; there's no eclipse and no hidden sun there. The darkness Krishna makes comes from the longer vulgate that Ganguli translates, which is what our film follows.", "timestamp": 1794171506, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "mannoj_gahlot", "author_id": "57147316536", "id": "18017050856755521", "text": "कृष्ण ने हर बार ऐसा ही किया है। चाहे कर्ण हो या जयद्रथ, दोनों को धोखे से मारा है—किसी राजनेता की तरह, हर बार धर्म का सहारा लेकर। धर्म की स्थापना के लिए छल का सहारा लेना कदापि अनुचित नहीं है..!", "timestamp": 1794108717, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "vedastovikings", "author_id": "60997589521", "id": "18096587540691546", "text": "@zen_paradoxx The passage we followed is Ganguli's Drona Parva 145: Krishna tells Arjuna his plan, makes the darkness by yoga, and lifts it after Jayadratha falls. Which passage are you using for the eclipse reading?", "timestamp": 1794056477, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "vedastovikings", "author_id": "60997589521", "id": "18131523454866793", "text": "@ayushrana4792 Fair question, and people in this thread clearly disagree on it. In the passage we filmed, Krishna tells Arjuna the plan first and makes the darkness while the sun is still up. Many readers weigh it against what was done to Abhimanyu the day before. Please keep the discussion about the text and the characters' choices.", "timestamp": 1794056462, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "vedastovikings", "author_id": "60997589521", "id": "18111906184922239", "text": "@aikantik07 Thanks for clarifying which edition you meant. In the Critical Edition, Drona Parva 7.121.15–16, Krishna tells Arjuna to strike as the sun is about to set. Those verses describe a sunset, not an eclipse. Which verse points you to a solar eclipse? Our reel follows Ganguli's section 145, where Krishna makes the darkness by yoga.", "timestamp": 1794056299, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "rajat.jain72", "author_id": "299584968", "id": "18134710021817064", "text": "Yes krishna was always right", "timestamp": 1794053970, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "priyanshujoshi285", "author_id": "12753663641", "id": "18060984953797537", "text": "Gamer vs developer", "timestamp": 1793723157, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "subham._.pradhan31", "author_id": "71359932717", "id": "18149199643565771", "text": "Radhe krishna ♥️", "timestamp": 1793708824, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "rose.petals.123", "author_id": "57098785355", "id": "18217066096361327", "text": "This is too good 🔥", "timestamp": 1793688521, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "aikantik07", "author_id": "61182003159", "id": "18109428626213308", "text": "wrong\nKrishna did not hide the Sun\nit was a solar eclipse\nhe just helped to sync the timing", "timestamp": 1793686420, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "xd_dibyo", "author_id": "77493360055", "id": "17970929829192267", "text": "He taught how politics works but always stood by truth , not comparable to modern politicians using god for money", "timestamp": 1793648572, "like_count": 11}], "webpage_url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DfM1QQTpaI7/", "webpage_url_basename": "DfM1QQTpaI7", "webpage_url_domain": "instagram.com", "extractor": "Instagram", "extractor_key": "Instagram", "thumbnail": "https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.